   "subject": "Re: Heatchart with custom colours",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi bogu, some data to play with would be great. Something along these lines will get you there.<div><br></div><div><font face=\"&#39;Lucida Console&#39;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:16px\"><div>\n\ncars &lt;- ggplot(mtcars, aes(y=factor(cyl), x= mpg))</div><div>cars + stat_bin(aes(fill=..count..), </div><div>geom = &quot;tile&quot;, binwidth=3, position=&quot;identity&quot;) + </div><div>stat_bin(aes(label=..count..), </div>\n\n<div>geom = &quot;text&quot;, binwidth=3, position=&quot;identity&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\">Then look at geom_tile at </span><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\"><a href=\"http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/geom_tile.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/geom_tile.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792380256136000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Z6RbcTsZfxLrCNCJoPXeY\">http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/geom_tile.html</a> and scale_fill_*. You&#39;ve got different choices, look at </span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\"><a href=\"http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/scale_hue.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/scale_hue.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792380256136000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mUpo3zUe3ZLo7p3j3lCZP\">http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/scale_hue.html</a> for example.</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\">HTH</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\">.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;line-height:normal\"><br>\n\n</span></div></span></font><div>Luciano<br>\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2011/3/11 bogu <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">giris...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\n\nIs it possible to produce heatchart (not clustered heatmap) with user<br>\ndefined colors for certain data range.<br>\nFor ex:<br>\n<a href=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_39NGKVWYg3o/SyqbudJ1_FI/AAAAAAAAA_w/GFyjf4yB4_U/s1600-h/Screen+shot+2009-12-17+at+3.59.12+PM.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_39NGKVWYg3o/SyqbudJ1_FI/AAAAAAAAA_w/GFyjf4yB4_U/s1600-h/Screen%2Bshot%2B2009-12-17%2Bat%2B3.59.12%2BPM.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792380256136000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00Vn1scfcyOKZR3CgyP8bm\">http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_39NGKVWYg3o/SyqbudJ1_FI/AAAAAAAAA_w/GFyjf4yB4_U/s1600-h/Screen+shot+2009-12-17+at+3.59.12+PM.png</a><br>\n\n\n</blockquote></div></div></div>"
